-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) -- Part V Division 2A
-- (s.71AA to s.71AE). Based on content from the Western Australian
-- Legislation website at 2026-09-07, "Residential Tenancies Act 1987",
-- State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0.

§ `Part V - Termination of residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 2A - Special provisions about terminating tenant's interest on grounds of family violence`

§§§ `71AA. Terms used`

-- DVO and Family Court injunction take their meaning from the Acts
-- named in s.71AA. Those meanings are facts in this encoding.

§§§ `71AB. Notice of termination of tenant's interest on ground that tenant subject to family violence`

DECLARE `report of family violence` HAS
    `the report is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `completed by a person who has worked with the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the medical profession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the psychology profession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a social worker as defined in the Mental Health Act 2014 section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a person in charge of a women's refuge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is a prescribed person or of a prescribed class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `section 71AB notice` HAS
    `the notice is given to the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is during the tenancy period likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in a prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS A NUMBER
    `a DVO applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Family Court injunction or an application for a Family Court injunction applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy of a prosecution notice or indictment containing a charge relating to violence against the tenant or a court record of a conviction of the charge applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a report of family violence accompanies the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the report of family violence` IS A `report of family violence`

GIVEN report IS A `report of family violence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report is completed by a person listed in section 71AB(2)(d)` IF
        report's `completed by a person who has worked with the tenant`
    AND (
            report's `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the medical profession`
        OR  report's `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the psychology profession`
        OR  report's `the person is a social worker as defined in the Mental Health Act 2014 section 4`
        OR  report's `the person is a police officer`
        OR  report's `the person is a person in charge of a women's refuge`
        OR  report's `the person is a prescribed person or of a prescribed class of persons`
        )

GIVEN notice IS A `section 71AB notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accompanying document is a document required under section 71AB(2)` IF
        notice's `a DVO applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice`
    OR  notice's `a Family Court injunction or an application for a Family Court injunction applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice`
    OR  notice's `a copy of a prosecution notice or indictment containing a charge relating to violence against the tenant or a court record of a conviction of the charge applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice`
    OR  (
            notice's `a report of family violence accompanies the notice`
        AND notice's `the report of family violence`'s `the report is in the approved form`
        AND `the report is completed by a person listed in section 71AB(2)(d)` (notice's `the report of family violence`)
        )

-- s.71AB(1): a tenant may give the notice despite any other provision
-- of this Act or another written law or a requirement under a contract.

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71AB(1)
@export Decide whether a tenant may give notice of termination of the tenant's interest under s.71AB(1)
GIVEN notice IS A `section 71AB notice` @desc A proposed s.71AB notice. The ground is that the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is, during the tenancy period, likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence. The notice may be given despite any other provision of this Act, another written law, or a contract (including during a fixed term).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant may give notice under section 71AB(1)` IF
        notice's `the notice is given to the lessor`
    AND notice's `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement`
    AND notice's `the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is during the tenancy period likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence`

-- s.71AC(3): on review the court examines compliance with s.71AB,
-- and cannot examine whether the tenant or a dependant has been or
-- might be subject to family violence. Compliance is therefore the
-- form, accompanying document and 7-day period, not the ground.

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71AB
@export Decide whether the terminating tenant has complied with s.71AB in giving the notice
GIVEN notice IS A `section 71AB notice` @desc The s.71AB notice as given. For s.71AC review, compliance is: given to the lessor; of termination of the tenant's interest; in the prescribed form (s.67(2)); accompanied by at least one s.71AB(2) document applicable during the tenancy period; and not less than 7 days before the termination day. The family-violence ground is not examined.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` IF
        notice's `the notice is given to the lessor`
    AND notice's `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement`
    AND notice's `the notice is in a prescribed form`
    AND `the accompanying document is a document required under section 71AB(2)` notice
    AND notice's `days of notice before the termination day` AT LEAST 7

DECLARE `division 2A actor` IS ONE OF
    `the lessor`
    `the tenant`
    `the cotenant`

DECLARE `division 2A action` IS ONE OF
    `disclose information in a document provided under section 71AB(2) otherwise than in accordance with this Act or another written law`
    `keep information provided under section 71AB(2) in a secure manner so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so`
    `give a copy of a notice received under section 71AB(1) to each cotenant`
    `give a copy of a document provided under section 71AB(2) to a cotenant`

-- s.71AB(3).

GIVETH A DEONTIC `division 2A actor` `division 2A action`
`the lessor must not disclose information in a document provided under section 71AB(2)` MEANS
    PARTY `the lessor`
    SHANT `disclose information in a document provided under section 71AB(2) otherwise than in accordance with this Act or another written law`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the lessor` BECAUSE "disclosed information in a document provided under s.71AB(2) otherwise than in accordance with this Act or another written law"

§§§ `71AC. Review of notice of termination under s. 71AB`

DECLARE `section 71AC review` HAS
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB` IS A NUMBER
    `the terminating tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71AC(2)
@export Decide whether the lessor may apply to a competent court to review whether a s.71AB notice was validly given
GIVEN review IS A `section 71AC review` @desc Days after the lessor received the s.71AB notice (the lessor may apply within 7 days), and whether the terminating tenant has complied with s.71AB in giving the notice. On review the court cannot examine whether the tenant or a dependant has been or might be subject to family violence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor may apply to review whether notice was validly given under section 71AB` IF
        review's `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB` AT MOST 7
    AND review's `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB` AT LEAST 0

GIVEN review IS A `section 71AC review`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must make an order declaring that the terminating tenant's interest has not been terminated` IF
    NOT review's `the terminating tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice`

GIVEN review IS A `section 71AC review`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must dismiss the application` IF
    review's `the terminating tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice`

§§§ `71AD. Rights of cotenants after notice under s. 71AB`

DECLARE `section 71AD facts` HAS
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB(1)` IS A NUMBER
    `the lessor has given a copy of the notice to each cotenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after giving the copy of the notice` IS A NUMBER
    `the cotenant received the copy of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the cotenant received the copy of the notice` IS A NUMBER
    `the cotenant has given notice of termination of the cotenant's interest to the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cotenant's notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cotenant's notice is signed by the cotenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cotenant's notice identifies the premises the subject of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cotenant's notice specifies the day on which the cotenant will deliver up possession of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS A NUMBER

-- s.71AD(2): the lessor must give a copy of the notice (not the
-- s.71AB(2) documents) to each cotenant within 7 days.

GIVETH A DEONTIC `division 2A actor` `division 2A action`
`the lessor must give a copy of the notice to each cotenant` MEANS
    PARTY `the lessor`
    MUST `give a copy of a notice received under section 71AB(1) to each cotenant`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the lessor` BECAUSE "did not give a copy of a notice received under s.71AB(1) to each cotenant within 7 days after receiving the notice"

-- s.71AD(3): nothing requires or permits the lessor to give a copy of
-- a s.71AB(2) document to a cotenant.

GIVETH A DEONTIC `division 2A actor` `division 2A action`
`the lessor must not give a copy of a document provided under section 71AB(2) to a cotenant` MEANS
    PARTY `the lessor`
    SHANT `give a copy of a document provided under section 71AB(2) to a cotenant`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the lessor` BECAUSE "gave a copy of a document provided under s.71AB(2) to a cotenant"

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71AD(4)
@export Decide whether a cotenant may give notice of termination of the cotenant's interest under s.71AD(4)
GIVEN facts IS A `section 71AD facts` @desc After a s.71AB(1) notice: whether the cotenant received a copy of that notice (not the accompanying s.71AB(2) documents), and how many days after receiving the copy. The cotenant may give notice within 7 days after receiving the copy.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cotenant may give notice of termination of the cotenant's interest` IF
        facts's `the cotenant received the copy of the notice`
    AND facts's `days after the cotenant received the copy of the notice` AT MOST 7
    AND facts's `days after the cotenant received the copy of the notice` AT LEAST 0

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71AD(4)-(5)
@export Decide whether a cotenant's notice of termination of the cotenant's interest under s.71AD(4) is effectual
GIVEN facts IS A `section 71AD facts` @desc The cotenant's s.71AD(4) notice. It must be given within 7 days after receiving the copy of the s.71AB(1) notice, be in the s.67(1) form (writing, signed, identifies the premises, specifies the possession day), and give not less than 21 days before the termination day.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the cotenant's notice under section 71AD(4) is effectual` IF
        `the cotenant may give notice of termination of the cotenant's interest` facts
    AND facts's `the cotenant has given notice of termination of the cotenant's interest to the lessor`
    AND facts's `the cotenant's notice is in writing`
    AND facts's `the cotenant's notice is signed by the cotenant`
    AND facts's `the cotenant's notice identifies the premises the subject of the agreement`
    AND facts's `the cotenant's notice specifies the day on which the cotenant will deliver up possession of the premises`
    AND facts's `days of notice before the termination day` AT LEAST 21

GIVEN facts IS A `section 71AD facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor gave a copy of the notice to each cotenant within 7 days` IF
        facts's `the lessor has given a copy of the notice to each cotenant`
    AND facts's `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB(1)` AT MOST 7
    AND facts's `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB(1)` AT LEAST 0

§§§ `71AE. Termination of tenant's interest by court on grounds of family violence`

-- family violence order means a DVO, Family Court injunction or other
-- court order denying a tenant's right of occupancy in the premises.

DECLARE `section 71AE application` HAS
    `the applicant is the excluded tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is a protected tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is a prescribed person acting on behalf of the protected tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a family violence order is in force against the excluded tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the excluded tenant has during the tenancy period committed family violence against the protected tenant or a dependant of the protected tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has considered the best interests of any child ordinarily resident at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has considered the best interests of the protected tenant including, if the premises are social housing premises, the ability of the tenant to meet any eligibility criteria for those premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has considered the effect the order might have on the lessor and any tenants other than the protected tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has considered the effect the order might have on any pets kept on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has considered the fact that perpetrators of family violence might seek to misuse the protections offered to tenants and lessors under this Act to further their violence and the need to prevent that misuse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are under this Act or the Act under which the family violence order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the order is made on which the order is specified to take effect` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN application IS A `section 71AE application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is a person who may apply under section 71AE(3)` IF
        application's `the applicant is the excluded tenant`
    OR  application's `the applicant is a protected tenant`
    OR  application's `the applicant is a prescribed person acting on behalf of the protected tenant`

GIVEN application IS A `section 71AE application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court is satisfied of a ground in section 71AE(2)` IF
        application's `a family violence order is in force against the excluded tenant`
    OR  application's `the excluded tenant has during the tenancy period committed family violence against the protected tenant or a dependant of the protected tenant`

GIVEN application IS A `section 71AE application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court has considered the matters in section 71AE(4)` IF
        application's `the court has considered the best interests of any child ordinarily resident at the premises`
    AND application's `the court has considered the best interests of the protected tenant including, if the premises are social housing premises, the ability of the tenant to meet any eligibility criteria for those premises`
    AND application's `the court has considered the effect the order might have on the lessor and any tenants other than the protected tenant`
    AND application's `the court has considered the effect the order might have on any pets kept on the premises`
    AND application's `the court has considered the fact that perpetrators of family violence might seek to misuse the protections offered to tenants and lessors under this Act to further their violence and the need to prevent that misuse`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71AE
@export Decide whether the court may make an order terminating a tenant's interest under s.71AE
GIVEN application IS A `section 71AE application` @desc An application to terminate an excluded tenant's interest. Standing: the excluded tenant, a protected tenant, or a prescribed person acting on behalf of the protected tenant. Ground: a family violence order (DVO, Family Court injunction or other court order denying occupancy) is in force against the excluded tenant, or the excluded tenant has during the tenancy period committed family violence against the protected tenant or a dependant. Before making the order the court must consider the s.71AE(4) matters, with the best interests of any child ordinarily resident as of primary importance. Proceedings may be under this Act or the Act under which the family violence order is made.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order terminating a tenant's interest under section 71AE` IF
        `the applicant is a person who may apply under section 71AE(3)` application
    AND `the court is satisfied of a ground in section 71AE(2)` application
    AND `the court has considered the matters in section 71AE(4)` application
    AND application's `the proceedings are under this Act or the Act under which the family violence order is made`

GIVEN application IS A `section 71AE application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified day on which the order takes effect is within the permitted range` IF
        application's `days after the order is made on which the order is specified to take effect` AT LEAST 7
    AND application's `days after the order is made on which the order is specified to take effect` AT MOST 30

§§ `Fixtures`

`empty report` MEANS `report of family violence` WITH
    `the report is in the approved form` IS FALSE,
    `completed by a person who has worked with the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the medical profession` IS FALSE,
    `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the psychology profession` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a social worker as defined in the Mental Health Act 2014 section 4` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a police officer` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a person in charge of a women's refuge` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a prescribed person or of a prescribed class of persons` IS FALSE

`police report` MEANS `report of family violence` WITH
    `the report is in the approved form` IS TRUE,
    `completed by a person who has worked with the tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the medical profession` IS FALSE,
    `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Western Australia) in the psychology profession` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a social worker as defined in the Mental Health Act 2014 section 4` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a police officer` IS TRUE,
    `the person is a person in charge of a women's refuge` IS FALSE,
    `the person is a prescribed person or of a prescribed class of persons` IS FALSE

`valid 71AB notice with DVO` MEANS `section 71AB notice` WITH
    `the notice is given to the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is during the tenancy period likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in a prescribed form` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS 7,
    `a DVO applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS TRUE,
    `a Family Court injunction or an application for a Family Court injunction applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a copy of a prosecution notice or indictment containing a charge relating to violence against the tenant or a court record of a conviction of the charge applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a report of family violence accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `the report of family violence` IS `empty report`

`71AB notice without document` MEANS `section 71AB notice` WITH
    `the notice is given to the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is during the tenancy period likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in a prescribed form` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS 7,
    `a DVO applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a Family Court injunction or an application for a Family Court injunction applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a copy of a prosecution notice or indictment containing a charge relating to violence against the tenant or a court record of a conviction of the charge applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a report of family violence accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `the report of family violence` IS `empty report`

`71AB notice of 6 days` MEANS `section 71AB notice` WITH
    `the notice is given to the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is during the tenancy period likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in a prescribed form` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS 6,
    `a DVO applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS TRUE,
    `a Family Court injunction or an application for a Family Court injunction applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a copy of a prosecution notice or indictment containing a charge relating to violence against the tenant or a court record of a conviction of the charge applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a report of family violence accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `the report of family violence` IS `empty report`

`71AB notice with police report` MEANS `section 71AB notice` WITH
    `the notice is given to the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is of termination of the tenant's interest in the residential tenancy agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant or a dependant of the tenant is during the tenancy period likely to be subjected or exposed to family violence` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in a prescribed form` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS 7,
    `a DVO applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a Family Court injunction or an application for a Family Court injunction applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a copy of a prosecution notice or indictment containing a charge relating to violence against the tenant or a court record of a conviction of the charge applicable during the tenancy period accompanies the notice` IS FALSE,
    `a report of family violence accompanies the notice` IS TRUE,
    `the report of family violence` IS `police report`

`timely 71AC review of a valid notice` MEANS `section 71AC review` WITH
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB` IS 7,
    `the terminating tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` IS TRUE

`timely 71AC review of an invalid notice` MEANS `section 71AC review` WITH
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB` IS 3,
    `the terminating tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` IS FALSE

`late 71AC review` MEANS `section 71AC review` WITH
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB` IS 8,
    `the terminating tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` IS TRUE

`cotenant 21 day notice on day 7` MEANS `section 71AD facts` WITH
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB(1)` IS 5,
    `the lessor has given a copy of the notice to each cotenant` IS TRUE,
    `days after giving the copy of the notice` IS 5,
    `the cotenant received the copy of the notice` IS TRUE,
    `days after the cotenant received the copy of the notice` IS 7,
    `the cotenant has given notice of termination of the cotenant's interest to the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice is in writing` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice is signed by the cotenant` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice identifies the premises the subject of the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice specifies the day on which the cotenant will deliver up possession of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS 21

`cotenant 20 day notice` MEANS `section 71AD facts` WITH
    `days after the lessor received the notice under section 71AB(1)` IS 5,
    `the lessor has given a copy of the notice to each cotenant` IS TRUE,
    `days after giving the copy of the notice` IS 5,
    `the cotenant received the copy of the notice` IS TRUE,
    `days after the cotenant received the copy of the notice` IS 7,
    `the cotenant has given notice of termination of the cotenant's interest to the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice is in writing` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice is signed by the cotenant` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice identifies the premises the subject of the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the cotenant's notice specifies the day on which the cotenant will deliver up possession of the premises` IS TRUE,
    `days of notice before the termination day` IS 20

`protected tenant 71AE application` MEANS `section 71AE application` WITH
    `the applicant is the excluded tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the applicant is a protected tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the applicant is a prescribed person acting on behalf of the protected tenant` IS FALSE,
    `a family violence order is in force against the excluded tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the excluded tenant has during the tenancy period committed family violence against the protected tenant or a dependant of the protected tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the court has considered the best interests of any child ordinarily resident at the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the best interests of the protected tenant including, if the premises are social housing premises, the ability of the tenant to meet any eligibility criteria for those premises` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the effect the order might have on the lessor and any tenants other than the protected tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the effect the order might have on any pets kept on the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the fact that perpetrators of family violence might seek to misuse the protections offered to tenants and lessors under this Act to further their violence and the need to prevent that misuse` IS TRUE,
    `the proceedings are under this Act or the Act under which the family violence order is made` IS TRUE,
    `days after the order is made on which the order is specified to take effect` IS 7

`71AE application with no ground` MEANS `section 71AE application` WITH
    `the applicant is the excluded tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the applicant is a protected tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the applicant is a prescribed person acting on behalf of the protected tenant` IS FALSE,
    `a family violence order is in force against the excluded tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the excluded tenant has during the tenancy period committed family violence against the protected tenant or a dependant of the protected tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the court has considered the best interests of any child ordinarily resident at the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the best interests of the protected tenant including, if the premises are social housing premises, the ability of the tenant to meet any eligibility criteria for those premises` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the effect the order might have on the lessor and any tenants other than the protected tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the effect the order might have on any pets kept on the premises` IS TRUE,
    `the court has considered the fact that perpetrators of family violence might seek to misuse the protections offered to tenants and lessors under this Act to further their violence and the need to prevent that misuse` IS TRUE,
    `the proceedings are under this Act or the Act under which the family violence order is made` IS TRUE,
    `days after the order is made on which the order is specified to take effect` IS 7

#EVAL `the tenant may give notice under section 71AB(1)` `valid 71AB notice with DVO`
#EVAL `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `valid 71AB notice with DVO`
#EVAL `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `71AB notice without document`
#EVAL `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `71AB notice of 6 days`
#EVAL `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `71AB notice with police report`
#EVAL `the lessor may apply to review whether notice was validly given under section 71AB` `timely 71AC review of a valid notice`
#EVAL `the court must dismiss the application` `timely 71AC review of a valid notice`
#EVAL `the court must make an order declaring that the terminating tenant's interest has not been terminated` `timely 71AC review of an invalid notice`
#EVAL `the lessor may apply to review whether notice was validly given under section 71AB` `late 71AC review`
#EVAL `the cotenant's notice under section 71AD(4) is effectual` `cotenant 21 day notice on day 7`
#EVAL `the cotenant's notice under section 71AD(4) is effectual` `cotenant 20 day notice`
#EVAL `the court may make an order terminating a tenant's interest under section 71AE` `protected tenant 71AE application`
#EVAL `the specified day on which the order takes effect is within the permitted range` `protected tenant 71AE application`
#EVAL `the court may make an order terminating a tenant's interest under section 71AE` `71AE application with no ground`
#ASSERT `the tenant may give notice under section 71AB(1)` `valid 71AB notice with DVO` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `valid 71AB notice with DVO` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `71AB notice without document` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `71AB notice of 6 days` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the tenant has complied with section 71AB in giving the notice` `71AB notice with police report` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court must dismiss the application` `timely 71AC review of a valid notice` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court must make an order declaring that the terminating tenant's interest has not been terminated` `timely 71AC review of an invalid notice` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the lessor may apply to review whether notice was validly given under section 71AB` `late 71AC review` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the cotenant's notice under section 71AD(4) is effectual` `cotenant 21 day notice on day 7` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cotenant's notice under section 71AD(4) is effectual` `cotenant 20 day notice` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the court may make an order terminating a tenant's interest under section 71AE` `protected tenant 71AE application` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may make an order terminating a tenant's interest under section 71AE` `71AE application with no ground` EQUALS FALSE

#TRACE `the lessor must not disclose information in a document provided under section 71AB(2)` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the lessor` DOES `disclose information in a document provided under section 71AB(2) otherwise than in accordance with this Act or another written law` AT 1

#TRACE `the lessor must give a copy of the notice to each cotenant` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the lessor` DOES `give a copy of a notice received under section 71AB(1) to each cotenant` AT 5

#TRACE `the lessor must give a copy of the notice to each cotenant` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the lessor` DOES `give a copy of a notice received under section 71AB(1) to each cotenant` AT 10

#TRACE `the lessor must not give a copy of a document provided under section 71AB(2) to a cotenant` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the lessor` DOES `give a copy of a document provided under section 71AB(2) to a cotenant` AT 1
